Description: firmware and IoT image identification and extraction tool
 moria identifies files and embedded content in firmware and IoT images and
 extracted rootfs trees, with confidence scores and sourced metadata as JSON.
 It can extract common embedded filesystems (SquashFS, ext2/3/4, F2FS, UBIFS,
 JFFS2, cramfs, EROFS, romfs, YAFFS2 and more), archives and boot/image
 containers, reverse some known vendor payload obfuscation, and carve raw byte
 ranges to disk. It never spawns a subprocess and makes no network calls.
 .
 The tool is built for use during IoT and embedded security assessments, where
 fast structured identification of every file in an unpacked firmware tree is
 the core value. The installed command is "moria". The package is named
 "moria-fw" because the name "moria" is already taken in Debian by an unrelated
 game.
